Class CatalogSlugNameRewriter:
- build a current-game slug-to-display-name map from the loaded CatalogSnapshot and requested ResponsePreferences
- compile one pattern for backticked canonical slugs and one for bare canonical slugs
- rewrite user-visible text by replacing matched canonical slugs with the preferred localized catalog name
- recursively rewrite AI result payload text while preserving structured identifier fields such as `*_slug`, `recommended_build_order`, build arrays, and rune arrays
- create a streaming rewriter that buffers enough text to avoid splitting a slug across SSE chunks

Class CatalogSlugNameStreamRewriter:
- accept visible text deltas from the streaming parser
- keep a short pending tail based on the longest known slug
- emit only text that cannot be part of an incomplete slug token, after applying the same localized replacement
- flush the remaining pending text when the stream display section is complete

Function _is_structured_identifier_key:
- classify result keys that must keep canonical machine-readable identifiers unchanged

Function _rewind_to_slug_boundary:
- move a streaming cutoff left until it is no longer inside a slug-like token
